---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-11-23-founders-pricing-layout.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-11-23',
  title: 'Founders application page says each point once, with the form always in reach',
  tags: ['waitlist', 'founders', 'pricing', 'layout'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">November 23, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    <a href="/pricing" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/pricing</a>, the Founders'
    Program application page, is rebuilt so each point appears once instead of three times.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Why</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The benefits, the 60-minute intro call and the 14-day hold each appeared in several places,
      which made the page long and repetitive. The video and real reviews now come before the
      detail, and the application form stays in reach the whole time.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">What changed</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>On desktop the form sits beside the content and stays in view while the page scrolls; there are no apply buttons in the content. On phones one Apply For A Founding Spot button under the video jumps to the form, which follows the content.</li>
      <li>The intro-call video shows unboxed with one headline, Why Become a Founder and Book an Intro Call?, and a single line under it pointing to the live demo.</li>
      <li>Three reviews (Farmstead 51, VonDoodles and an App Store review) replace the rotating carousel, with a link to all reviews.</li>
      <li>Only For Breeders Who Join Before Launch and What We Commit To are merged into one list.</li>
      <li>The four steps carry the 60-minute call and the 14-day hold, so the separate What Happens Next block is gone, on the page and inside the form.</li>
      <li>Removed: the Not Sure An Hour Is Worth It? card (page and form) with its walkthrough dialog, the phone-only summary cards, the line about going over pricing on the call, and three of the Probably Not The Right Time If points.</li>
      <li>Sections are separated by spacing and headings; only the steps and the form remain cards. The form's fields, validation and submission are unchanged.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</article>
